Workstream ID: navigation-refinements
Title: Add a shared current-date display and refine navigation order
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Provide a locally reviewable, readable navigation refinement
Dependencies: None
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/27
Purpose: Show the browser-local current month, centered day number and weekday
  in the persistent header. Place Daily plan immediately below Overview.
  Preserve existing controls, readable typography and saved records.
  The owner explicitly requests local review before publication.

Tasks:
  [x] Inspect the shared shell, local-date lifecycle and responsive layout.
  [x] Reuse the current workspace date without adding another clock or storage.
  [x] Place Daily plan directly after Overview without changing route identities.
  [x] Replace the rejected orbital treatment with a quiet paper-calendar tile.
  [x] Spread month/day/weekday across a wider responsive composition.
  [x] Enlarge month/weekday text and the central date after owner feedback.
  [x] Bring the labels closer and add a restrained paper hover effect.
  [x] Make only the calendar's top strip red on local Saturdays and Sundays.
  [x] Qualify the current paper version's local date, layout and finite animation.
  [x] Check existing search, theme, navigation and graph viewport behavior.
  [x] Update focused documentation and prepare same-identity tracking/continuity.
  [x] Prepare the running current-source local preview for owner review.

Acceptance criteria:
  Normal pages share one date display: month left, day number centered and
    weekday right, with an accessible complete local calendar date.
  Both themes and narrow layouts retain the full date and existing controls
    without overlap, clipped text, smaller typography or horizontal overflow.
  A recognizable paper-calendar date has generous spacing and larger labels.
    No orbits, stars, glow, trails, looping decoration or extra motion button.
    Only a brief page turn on initial load or an actual date change; reduced
    motion remains authoritative and open native dialogs suspend that turn.
  Labels stay near the tile at 24px, with readable 21px standard abbreviations
    on narrow screens and the complete accessible date retained. The day is
    48px. Hover gives the paper a gentle lift/tilt and shadow, not ambient noise.
  Saturday and Sunday use a red top strip in both themes; weekdays retain teal.
    The rule follows the browser-local date and updates through midnight.
  Existing local-day updates keep the date current across midnight, including
    month/year changes and tutorial practice, without a second timer.
  Daily plan immediately follows Overview in desktop and compact navigation;
    its route, tutorial target and saved plans remain unchanged.
  The graph still fits the available viewport below the responsive header.
  No new progress/reward, schema, dependency, workflow or browser-record change.
  Tests use disposable fictional browser contexts, never the owner's profile.
  Local technical verification is separate from pending human review.
  No staging, commit, push or deployment; the published website stays unchanged.

